1874	///
1875	/// Join conjuncts resolve through `slot_global_index` over the concatenated child rows using
1876	/// DESCRIPTOR materialized widths; a carried (wider-than-descriptor) child would physically
1877	/// shift every right-side column while the descriptor math would not — a wrong column read,
1878	/// not a type error the engine would catch. Consumers of a common slot across a join are
1879	/// therefore refused, loudly, at translation.
1880	fn refuse_carried_join_child(node: &TPlanNode, child: &TranslatedRel) -> Result<()> {
